  contentsAnswer: An overnight change of clothes. I am driving straight on after
    breakfast.
  weightAnswer: Four or five kilos. Just a shirt, towel and soft things.
  metalAnswer: No tools, no electronics. I travel light.
  packingAnswer: Everything is under the straps. Nothing loose or powered.
  responseAnswer: The clothes must have settled. The road has been rough tonight.
  authorReasoning: 'Carrier: 12.9 kg conflicts with the confident light-load claim;
    delayed sustained corrective pulse conflicts with strapped soft clothing. Two
    independent contradictions.'
